# Authentication vs authorization

## Plugin semantics

Authentication establishes identity. Authorization (separate plugin/concern) decides permissions. This pack must not invent policy frameworks.

## Required behavior

- If the task is “can user X edit record Y?”, check whether `cakephp/authorization` is installed before recommending policies.
- If Authorization is absent, follow existing project permission patterns — do not invent Gate/Policy APIs.
- Never equate “authenticated” with “authorized for this resource.”

## Anti-patterns

- Role checks scattered only in login listeners as the sole permission model without project convention
- Recommending `Authorization->authorize` when the package is not present
